            <ArticleTitle>[A pregnant woman with a painful abdominal retraction].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>A8090</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 35-year old woman, gravida 2, para 1, came to our hospital with abdominal pain and a retraction of her abdomen, which appeared during her spontaneous contractions at 40 weeks and 5 days of pregnancy. She had a medical history of caesarean section for Frank breech presentation. This clinical presentation was suggestive for uterine rupture, which was confirmed during caesarean section.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
